Wings patch 0017: pass MCP servers' own usage notes to the model

MCP servers can send `instructions` when a client connects: how their
tools fit together, what to call first, limits. OpenManus passes them to
the model. Upstream called session.initialize() and discarded the result,
so agents used such servers with less guidance.

  * src/mcp_manager.py: stdio, SSE and HTTP connections keep the
    instructions (cleaned of control and hidden characters and capped at
    1,500 characters by wings/mcp_notes.py); the MCP tool catalog in the
    prompt shows them under that server's name, labelled as the server's
    words that never override the user or the agent's rules. Approval
    gates and per agent tool access apply exactly as before.

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (same as upstream)

